    50	1According  to Google  Scholar,  August  2024.observing  the output  and the tester providing  feedback  to the search-
    51	based system  based on candidate  solutions.  In our solution  proposal,  we
    52	follow  this human-in-the-loop  approach  outlined  by [1]. To assess and
    53	react appropriately  to the output  of the LLM-system,  it is essential  that
    54	reviewers  (a) are well educated  in using the mapping  study method,
    55	and (b) be experts  in the topic they are reviewing.
    56	Khalil et al. [2] reviewed  machine  learning  tools for literature  stud-
    57	ies. The tools were assessed  prior to ChatGPT’s  release.  Therefore,  the
    58	tools required  manual  labeling  (e.g. during  paper screening),  whereas
    59	a LLM like ChatGPT  can produce  a descriptive  assessment  outcome  in-
    60	cluding  rationales  and text fragments.  Similarly,  the framework  by [3]
    61	focusing  on paper screening  needed  to be trained  based on the users’
    62	labels.
    63	2. LLM-supported  mapping  process
    64	This section  discusses  how to incorporate  LLMs in every step of the
    65	mapping  process,  which is presented  in [4].Fig. 1presents  each step
    66	of the review  process  and briefly  outlines  the input and actions  done
    67	by the user and the output  of the LLM. For all the steps outlined  below
    68	we would  like to highlight  that the researcher  should  have an initial
    69	idea of possible  search  terms,  inclusion  criteria  or extraction  items in
    70	order to validate  the outputs.  Specifically,  research  problems  and goals
    71	should  be driven  by relevant  practical  needs.
